  "Dividend Portfolio Best Practices": "高配当株ポートフォリオの選び方",
  "Look for Dividend Aristocrats": "連続増配銘柄（配当貴族）に着目",
  "Focus on companies with 25+ consecutive years of increasing dividend payments, which proves durable competitive advantages.": "25年以上連続で増配を続けている企業は、景気後退期でも安定したキャッシュフローと競争優位性を持っています。",
  "Check the Payout Ratio": "配当性向の健全性チェック",
  "A payout ratio below 60% indicates a safe, sustainable dividend with room for future growth, whereas ratios above 85% signal risk of dividend cuts.": "配当性向が40〜60%程度であれば持続可能性が高く、80%を超える極端に高い銘柄は減配リスクがあります。",
  "Tax Location Optimization": "NISAを活用した配当非課税化",
  "Hold high-yielding dividend stocks and REITs inside tax-advantaged accounts (like Roth IRAs) to avoid annual dividend income tax drag.": "通常約20.315%かかる配当課税を、新NISAの成長投資枠を活用して非課税で受け取ります。",
  // === inflation ===
  "Understanding Inflation & Protecting Purchasing Power": "インフレの脅威と購買力防衛の知恵",
  "Inflation is the steady rise in prices over time, acting as an invisible tax that erodes the purchasing power of idle cash. Beating inflation is the primary prerequisite of wealth accumulation.": "インフレ（物価上昇）は現金の実質的な価値を静かに削り取る「見えない税金」です。資産形成においてインフレヘッジは不可欠です。",
  "The Consumer Price Index & The Rule of 72": "消費者物価指数（CPI）と72の法則",
  "Inflation is tracked through consumer price indices (CPI) that monitor a representative basket of goods and services. Using the Rule of 72, dividing 72 by a 3% inflation rate shows that living expenses double roughly every 24 years.": "72をインフレ率で割ることで、物価が2倍になる年数がわかります（例：年3%インフレなら72÷3＝24年で物価が2倍）。",
  "Future Purchasing Power Formula": "将来の購買力低下の計算",
